        <title type="html"><![CDATA[[WebExtensions] Limits for alarms.create()]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29521</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29521"/>
        <updated>2026-04-21T20:16:15.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45960703?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Document limits for <code class="notranslate">alarms.create()</code>.</p>

<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<p dir="auto">Chrome limits amount of storage which extension alarms can consume:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Chrome 117 limited extensions to 500 alarms each. This is already described in the MDN article[1] and Chromium source[2].</li>
<li>Chrome 150 will limit lengths of new alarm names to 1024 bytes.
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Chrome 148 logs an error if extension calls <code class="notranslate">alarms.create(name, ...)</code> with a name longer than 1024 bytes.[3]</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">[1] <a href="https://github.com/mdn/content/blob/main/files/en-us/mozilla/add-ons/webextensions/api/alarms/create/index.md">https://github.com/mdn/content/blob/main/files/en-us/mozilla/add-ons/webextensions/api/alarms/create/index.md</a><br>
[2] <a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/96b950168c0f85db3738e0215e5126fc2b305227/hovercard" href="https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/96b950168c0f85db3738e0215e5126fc2b305227">chromium/chromium@<tt>96b9501</tt></a><br>
[3] <a class="commit-link" data-hovercard-type="commit" data-hovercard-url="https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/432c30e3e1dcd03cecb869a1e23162d8ea1b9af2/hovercard" href="https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/432c30e3e1dcd03cecb869a1e23162d8ea1b9af2">chromium/chromium@<tt>432c30e</tt></a></p>


